{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3462","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3462","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3462\",\"parent_revision\":\"86a6b0a6b11f896184b823541c8e6af9771eeb5b387b064cbc2abe54e794fc2f\",\"root_revision\":\"86a6b0a6b11f896184b823541c8e6af9771eeb5b387b064cbc2abe54e794fc2f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA finding that the architecture is wrong is the most expensive kind to discover late, and it currently has nowhere to go \u2014 the agent that finds it can only fail the task it was doing. A change can complete with its documentation unupdated and no step responsible for noticing. And because Design and Plan share a stage and an artifact, the adversarial challenge the architecture requires of a design has no separate output to be recorded in or checked against.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Is Missing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/ARCHITECTURE.md` specifies the workflow. Three stages it specifies have no implementation that matches. These were briefly narrated inside the architecture document itself, which was the wrong place \u2014 a specification states the design, and conformance belongs in tracked work \u2014 so they are recorded here instead.\\n\\n### Loop does not route by cause\\n\\nThe architecture states that a finding is routed by what caused it: an architectural issue reaches Design, which then reaches Plan to consider what changes; an environmental or external factor reaches Plan directly.\\n\\nWhat exists is two loop-back edges scoped to a verdict \u2014 a `NEEDS_WORK` return in `skills/forensic-review` for one task, and a `NOT_CERTIFIED` return in `skills/final-verification` for one feature. An architectural finding surfaced during work has no route to Design, and an environmental one no route to Plan; the reviewing agent can only return the task that surfaced it.\\n\\n### Closure checks are not conditional on what changed\\n\\nThe architecture states that the end of the graph reviews the whole changeset in proportion to what changed \u2014 code review where code changed, prose review where prose was edited, a check that reports exist and outcomes were met where the work evaluated a system \u2014 and updates documentation.\\n\\n`BookendType` in `sam_schema/core/models.py` admits `t0-baseline` and `tn-verification` and nothing else. A grep of `skills/` and `agents/` for a documentation-check step at the end of a graph returns nothing. `agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` exists and is referenced from `skills/complete-implementation` and `skills/create-artifact`, but not as a structural step on a plan's graph, so no plan requires a documentation check to have happened.\\n\\n### Design is not a distinct stage\\n\\nThe architecture describes Design (produce architecture, then adversarially challenge it) and Plan (work out how to achieve it and how to prove it was achieved) as separate stages with separate outputs.\\n\\nBoth are carried by `skills/planning`, which produces a single `architect` artifact. There is no architect skill or agent; the only `architect`-named skill is `code-review-architecture`, which is a code-review specialisation and not this stage.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/ARCHITECTURE.md` (the specification), against `plugins/development-harness/skills/` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/` (the implementation).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThese are conformance gaps between a specification and its implementation, not defects in either taken alone. Closing them means either building the stages or amending the architecture, and which of those is right is a grooming question rather than a settled one.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"86814799fd465134dece94a693cc4da59d6f3c827051b5ee7008fbe317181033\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyf3w\"}"}